<<~ ahu slot=`#/purpose`>>

!! The Floor Queue

Only the familiar runs builds and tests on this box, one heavy run at a time (operator, 2026-11-25, after the second WSL VHD crash). The queue the familiar drains stands as one append log, `lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/state/test-floor`: `QUEUE` enters a tasked spirit's hand-back, `RUN` and `WHY` carry its ticket body, `TAKE` marks the floor held, `DONE` lands the bench gate's verdict with its byte rows (`wrote=`, `c-drop=`), `DROP` sets a ticket down unrun. `[[<ledger>]floor-queue[<view>],[<arg>]]` answers each view: waiting, next, skip, taken, green, red, stopped, dropped, budget, ticket, runs, sha, green-sha.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/law`>>

!! The Queue Law Runs In The Wiki

The placement law (mandate/floor-gate-1): code that CAN live in the wiki VM MUST. The fold (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/floor-ledger.ts`) orders tickets by their place in the log, never by a clock; a QUEUE over a waiting ticket folds to nothing, and a waiting ticket whose sha already holds a GREEN verdict reads `skip`. The host tools (`tools/floor-ledger.mjs`, `tools/floor-run.mjs`) append lines through the tiddler door and ask through the render door; while the doors stand dark they append to the flat mirror `<passwd home>/.lares-scratch/.floor/queue.log`, and `node tools/floor-ledger.mjs otakiage` folds it back in. The host gates (the one flock, the floor-guard hook, the C: sampler, source-only benches, the docker build lock) stay in `tools/`, because they gate host processes.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/callers`>>

!! Callers

The floor page (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/tw5/floor/page`) renders the views; `tools/floor-run.mjs --ticket <id>` asks `skip` before it runs, and `tools/floor-ledger.mjs ask <view> [<arg>]` asks any view.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/caps-cost`>>

!! Caps and Cost

The operator reads through the wiki it runs in and writes nothing; one call folds the ledger once.

<<~/ahu>>

